.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD-CERT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd-cert
.Nd ocifbsd certificate management tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
tool manages X.509 certificates used by the
.Xr ocifbsd 8
OCI runtime.
It supports certificate authority (CA) creation, node enrollment,
automatic rotation, ACME/Let's Encrypt integration, and external
CA enrollment (SCEP, EST, ADCS, Vault PKI).
.Pp
Certificate data is stored under
.Pa /etc/ocifbsd/certs
with backups under
.Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/certs/backups .
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm list
List all known certificates as JSON to standard output.
.It Cm rotate
Rotate every certificate that is due for renewal.
.It Cm check
Verify every certificate's expiry and emit syslog alerts for
those approaching the warning or critical thresholds.
.It Cm backup Ar name
Create a timestamped backup of
.Ar name Ap s
key and certificate.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/lib/ocifbsd/certs/backups -compact
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/certs
Certificate storage directory.
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/certs/backups
Certificate backup directory.
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/certs/registry.json
On-disk registry of known certificates.
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/certs/history.log
Append-only audit log of certificate actions.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was developed by
.An REVYTECH, Inc.
